  "topic": "POL Review Heuristics",
  "content": "1. Anonymity: Verify explicit double-blind markers (e.g., 'Anonymous authors', 'Paper under double-blind review') and scan for self-identifying text, acknowledgments, or URLs. 2. Data Privacy: Assess datasets for PII; standard public benchmarks (e.g., MNIST) are generally compliant, but sensitive data requires explicit consent and anonymization evidence. 3. Broader Impact: Check for dedicated sections discussing societal, security, or ethical implications. Even for benign tasks, adversarial robustness research has security implications that should be addressed. 4. Ethics & Dual-Use: Identify dual-use potential (e.g., attack vs. defense) and ensure the paper discusses responsible deployment or potential harms. 5. Plagiarism: Verify proper citation of prior work and originality of empirical findings to rule out self-plagiarism or dual submission.",
  "reviewer_name": "POL Specialist",
  "reviewer_dimension": "POL"
}

